-- title:
--   Original finite-cap physical stopped Itô cash positive grid error, before Gaussian/marked-jump centring
-- statement:
--   For the original physical ruin-clipped Levy dividend surplus, fixed finite cap C, original stopped terminal F and genuine nonlinear negative-jump compensated marked integral J, and any residual R given by the actual intrinsic Gaussian truncated-residual path limit, there exists a finite bounded predictable stopped Gaussian grid whose signed stopped Ito-Stieltjes reward positive excess has integrable arbitrarily small expected value on every initial-filtration event. The exact post-right-dividend terminal, ruin-crossing jump, physical HJB drift and dividend paymentTimes convention are retained. Gaussian G and nonlinear J centring are NOT hypotheses: they are independently already Proved in d6b37ee9-d26c-4977-9419-38aa1434019e. This theorem is the genuine remaining stopped Ito-Meyer error estimate, not a tautological substitute or an assumed conclusion for its parent.
-- source:
--   Original Avram classical source, finite cap; independent original physical marked-J cash estimate; parent 3f363bfb-ba60-4ebb-b82f-b87c82744fc5

